            <title>Final prototype</title>
            <link>https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/p/final-prototype/</link>
            <pubDate>Thu, 09 Sep 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
            <guid>https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/p/final-prototype/</guid>
            <description>&lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/img/proto1.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Featured image of post Final prototype&#34; /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Final prototype&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;September 5, 2021&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Finally after more than a year and a half, I finished my industrial prototype. As I mentioned before, the unit should have been 16 feet long in order to be as productive as possible (length of panels normally). I was running out of space, and wanted to save money, so I made a smaller one.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto1.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;The whole system&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            The whole system&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto2.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;The whole system side view&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            The whole system side view&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;center&gt;&#xA;&lt;video controls class=&#39;center&#39; video=&#39;this is a label&#39; controls=&#34;yes&#34; style=&#34;width: 65%; height: 65%; border:5px solid black;&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;source src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/total2.mp4&#34; type=&#34;video/mp4&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;p&gt; Your browser does not support video. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/video&gt;&#xA;&lt;/center&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p style=&#34;text-align:center;color:darkgray;font-size:125%;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;, Times, serif;font-weight:100d;&#34;&gt;Short video of the system&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The water control unit, where there are the ph and ppm sensors placed above it. The three small peristaltic pumps work when there is an imbalance of ph or ppm. there is a aquarium pump inside the basin to stir the water when a peristaltic pump sends its additive.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto3.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;Water control unit&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            Water control unit&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The inside of the mister unit where the roots are located. This unit is normally closed to make sure no alges will develop.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto4.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;Inside view of the mister unit&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            Inside view of the mister unit&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The motor and the sliding system. In the small black box it&amp;rsquo;s the temperature and humidity sensor.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto8.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;Motor and the sliding system&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            Motor and the sliding system&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;The control computer where it is possible to change parameters, such as motor speed, ppm level, ph level. It is also possible to stop and restart the stepper motor and the misters. The program also allows real-time monitoring of pressure ph, ppm, temperature and humidity data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto5.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;Control panel&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            Control panel&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;    &lt;figure &gt;&#xA;        &#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://olboi7.github.io/fantastic-waffle/img/proto7.jpg&#34;  style=&#34;border: 4px solid black; vertical-align:middle&#34; alt=&#34;Inside the control panel&#34; /&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &lt;p&gt;&#xA;            Inside the control panel&#xA;            &#xA;                &#xA;            &#xA;            &lt;/p&gt; &#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;</description>
        </item></channel>
